+## Proven through-cut profiles and Reference subtraction features (Nhip)
+
+The Nhip bridge repair distinguishes Reference subtraction features from real
+Body cuts. For a reconciled single extrusion with every cutter proven through,
+one complete planar difference handles boundary notches and disconnected
+components. A separate box proof handles sweeps authored along the plate length.
+Blind and oblique finite cuts use the same exact kernel in a bounded source
+frame, with authored cutter extents preserved. Source curves refine to a
+fraction of the participating Body context Precision; refined caches stay
+local. Independent cutters pack into bounded batches by cost, while overlapping
+cutters retain their authored order. There is no cutter expansion retry.
+
+Stored f32 closure is checked after each coordinate conversion, including the
+desktop packet basis. Only zero-area faces are removed from proven finite
+surfaces. Exact boundary subdivision uses existing collinear endpoints and
+preserves each receiving face's normals; it does not weld short positive
+features. An origin compensation can change the storage phase without changing
+the placed geometry. Commit a repair only after its exact closure proof passes.
+
+Five interleaved native base/branch pairs on the house control found a small
+total-time increase near the timer granularity, with identical ordered geometry
+fingerprints. The void-heavy
+ISSUE_129 cohort reduced geometry and total time with similar parse time.
+Its geometry intentionally differs: proven all-through slab cuts replace the
+old residual result, and independent IfcOpenShell comparisons confirmed the
+repaired hosts' closure and material volumes. The fixture still has pre-existing
+CSG failures elsewhere; this is not a claim of complete ISSUE_129 repair.
+Raw phase measurements, both fingerprints and changed output counts live under
+`scripts/perf/evidence/nhip-through-cuts-20261024/`.
+
+These are end-to-end native worker-pool measurements, not browser worker-pool
+or visible-frame claims. Agent-controlled builds and browser evidence sessions
+were closed for the interleaved run; unrelated user applications remained open.
+The heavy Holter/ISSUE_053 fixtures were absent locally. Lesson: validate the
+complete stored mesh after ordinary cleanup, and derive boundary tolerance
+from the participating representation context rather than scanning the whole
+model per native job or loosening a topology gate. A coarse oracle mesh can
+also exceed the authored Precision: confirm curved-reference convergence before
+attributing a volume discrepancy to the Boolean result. Canonical closure is
+not sufficient proof of final packet closure; audit the transmitted vertices.
+
